F:\GitHub\FunWasHad\docs\deployment\Docker-Server-Deploy.md:44:## CI Deployment To PAYTON-DESKTOP
F:\GitHub\FunWasHad\docs\deployment\Docker-Server-Deploy.md:46:GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines, and Octopus Deploy run the server stack deploy with `scripts/Invoke-PaytonDesktopDockerDeploy.ps1`. The script generates `.env.pipeline` from CI secrets, verifies it is running on `PAYTON-DESKTOP`, then calls the Nuke `DeployDockerServer` target with Docker Desktop's Linux engine. `NGROK_AUTHTOKEN` is a required secret: the compose stack recreates the `fwh-ngrok` container on every deploy, and an empty token crash-loops it (ERR_NGROK_4018) and takes `https://funwashad.ngrok.app` offline. The script fails fast when any required secret, including the ngrok token, is missing:
F:\GitHub\FunWasHad\docs\deployment\Docker-Server-Deploy.md:51:  -PublicBaseUrl http://PAYTON-DESKTOP:5080
F:\GitHub\FunWasHad\docs\deployment\Docker-Server-Deploy.md:54:Set `FWH_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` in CI variables to the current ngrok HTTPS URL when the deployed Marketing Admin/OIDC redirects need to use ngrok externally. If it is not set, pipelines deploy with `http://PAYTON-DESKTOP:5080`.
